.TH "ALTFSCHANGER" "8" "15 November 2026" "LTFS" "LTFS Command Reference"

.SH NAME
altfschanger \- Drive a tape library's medium changer through a changer plugin
.SH SYNOPSIS

\fBaltfschanger\fR [ \fB-e \fIname\fB\fR ] [ \fB-i \fIfile\fB\fR ] \fBlist\fR


\fBaltfschanger\fR \fB-d \fIname\fB\fR [ \fB-e \fIname\fB\fR ] [ \fB-i \fIfile\fB\fR ] [ \fB-o \fIoption\fB\fR ] [ \fB--verbose=\fInum\fB\fR ] [ \fB--ready-wait=\fIseconds\fB\fR ] [ \fB--move-wait=\fIseconds\fB\fR ] \fB\fIcommand\fB\fR [ \fB\fIargument\fB\fR\fI ...\fR ]

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBaltfschanger\fR sends single operations to the medium changer of a tape
library. It is a tool for testing the changer plugins and the changer layer and for
driving a library by hand; it keeps no state between runs.
.PP
The plugin commands go straight to the changer plugin and name elements by their
address as the changer reports it: they read the element status, move and exchange
cartridges, and make the changer re-read its elements. They check nothing.
.PP
The cartridge commands go through the changer layer and name cartridges by barcode and
drives by serial number (by element address on a changer that does not report drive
serial numbers). Each one reads the whole library first, reads the elements a move
touches right before the move, and prints the inventory when it succeeds. The library
is shared with its operator panel and with other hosts and is not reserved; the layer
re-reads what a unit attention says has changed and does not repeat a move whose
outcome is unknown.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB-d, --device=\fIname\fB\fR
The medium changer. Its form depends on the plugin: for the file
plugin, a library directory, or the name or serial number of a library directory
under the directory that the environment variable
\fBALTFS_FILE_CHANGER_ROOT\fR names.
.TP
\fB-e, --backend=\fIname\fB\fR
Use the specified changer plugin (default: the default changer of the configuration file)
.TP
\fB-i, --config=\fIfile\fB\fR
Use the specified configuration file
.TP
\fB-o \fIoption\fB\fR
Pass an option to the changer plugin; \fBaltfschanger help\fR lists them
.TP
\fB--verbose=\fInum\fB\fR
Set the log level: 0 errors, 1 warnings, 2 informational (the default),
3 to 6 debug.
.TP
\fB--ready-wait=\fIseconds\fB\fR
How long a cartridge command waits for a changer that is not ready (door open) before it fails (default: 30)
.TP
\fB--move-wait=\fIseconds\fB\fR
How long a cartridge may be in neither element of a move (on the picker) before the layer re-reads the library (default: 5)
.TP
\fB-h, --help\fR
Show the usage
.TP
\fB-V, --version\fR
Show the version
.SH "PLUGIN COMMANDS"
.TP
\fBlist\fR
List the medium changers this host can reach
.TP
\fBinfo\fR
Show the identity of the changer, its element address assignment and whether it reads barcodes, reports drive serial numbers and accepts EXCHANGE MEDIUM
.TP
\fBelements [\fItype\fB [\fIstart\fB [\fIcount\fB]]]\fR
Show the element status, one element per line: type, address, full or empty,
then voltag= (the barcode), source=,
dvcid= (the drive serial number) and the flags
inaccessible, except=\fIASC\fR/\fIASCQ\fR
and impexp\&. \fItype\fR is
transport, storage, ie,
drive or any (the default).
.TP
\fBmove \fIsource\fB \fIdest\fB [\fItransport\fB]\fR
MOVE MEDIUM from one element address to another
.TP
\fBexchange \fIsource\fB \fIdest1\fB \fIdest2\fB [\fItransport\fB]\fR
EXCHANGE MEDIUM: the cartridge at \fIsource\fR goes to \fIdest1\fR and the one at \fIdest1\fR goes to \fIdest2\fR, which may be \fIsource\fR
.TP
\fBscan [\fIstart\fB \fIcount\fB]\fR
Make the changer re-read its elements (INITIALIZE ELEMENT STATUS); on a large library this takes minutes
.TP
\fBtur\fR
Send TEST UNIT READY
.TP
\fBprevent, allow\fR
Lock or unlock the import/export station
.TP
\fBhelp\fR
Show the options of the changer plugin
.SH "CARTRIDGE COMMANDS"
.TP
\fBinventory\fR
Show the library (library line: identity, ready, stale, counts,
last unit attention), its drives (drive lines: serial, address,
what it holds) and its cartridges (tape lines: barcode, where,
address, state, home slot). Cartridges without a readable barcode are listed as
unlabeled\fIn\fR in address order.
.TP
\fBrescan [deep]\fR
Read every element again; deep makes the changer re-read its elements first
.TP
\fBload \fIbarcode\fB \fIdrive\fB\fR
Move the cartridge into the drive. A duplicate barcode, a cleaning cartridge (CLN) and a cartridge in the import/export station are refused.
.TP
\fBreturn \fIdrive\fB\fR
Move the cartridge in the drive back to the slot it came from, or to a free slot when that one is taken
.TP
\fBswap \fIbarcode\fB \fIdrive\fB\fR
Return the cartridge in the drive and load the other one, with EXCHANGE MEDIUM when the changer accepts it and two moves otherwise
.TP
\fBexport \fIbarcode\fB\fR
Move the cartridge to a free import/export element
.TP
\fBimport \fIbarcode\fB\fR
Move the cartridge from the import/export station to a free storage slot
.PP
The cartridge commands only move cartridges: they do not load the tape in the drive,
mount it or unload it.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.PP
0 on success, 8 when the operation failed (the message ACH0004E gives
the internal error code), 16 for a usage error.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
altfs(8), mkaltfs(8).
